+From 8ecbbbfa80f222f40cd36c5dff8e24049fa666b0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: kgw-ds <kgw-ds@users.noreply.github.com>
+Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 17:49:16 +0900
+Subject: [PATCH] BananaDS: kms.ff_music, the music at its own speed while
+ fast-forwarding
+
+While fast-forwarding, the game runs N times as fast and its music and
+sound effects keep their own tempo and pitch instead of fading out
+(kms.ff_mute) or playing sped up.
+
+- melonDS patch 0500: a sound clock. The ARM7's timers (the SDK's sound
+  alarm steps the sequencer on them) and the SPU run at a rate of the
+  game's time; exact under FastTimers and FastMix; 1.0 is melonDS's
+  paths; a DSi stays at 1.0.
+- ffmusic.h: each frame, the rate is 1 / the speed the game reaches
+  (frame times against the pacer's period, so Max and a slow game are
+  followed), nudged by the sound thread's backlog against
+  audio.servo_target. Host tests in tests.cpp.
+- frontend_kms: kms.ff_music (on) sets the clock while fast-forwarding
+  and leaves the sound unmuted; off, kms.ff_mute as before.
+- Emu::set_sound_clock, core.sound_clock (a fixed rate, for the tests).
+- CI: FastTimers and FastMix at scaled clocks against their slow paths
+  (dsreal, sndbench; x86 and aarch64 qemu), the clock changes the game's
+  state, and half the clock makes half the sound.
